<p>A few things that I dislike about this one, though the concept overall I do like.</p>
<p>1) This doesn't seem keter-class, as there doesn't seem to be any indication that this can't be easily contained by just putting it in a room somewhere and not touching it. Unless it somehow is able to activate itself, it seems that without the proper input it's just a big hunk of circuitry.</p>
<p>2) In the description, it's listed as being comprised of a laundry list of common items, and then [redacted], which is the cause of the anomalous behavior. It almost seems like a cop-out to not list what this last piece is. While on one hand it does have the whole &quot;mystery&quot; to it, on the other it's like describing a normal, every day object except for the [redacted] that makes it looks not normal. Maybe there's another way to of stating that there's an added piece that serves as the anomalous function?</p>

