			<div class="content" id="post-content-1471298">
									

<p>&quot;Special Containment Procedures: SCP-281 is currently contained within maximum security storage locker 18-E on level 7 of Site-76. SCP-281's lithium-ion battery pack is to remain plugged into Site-76's main power grid unless being used in testing.&quot;</p>
<p>That's what is done to keep it contained. It could sit there, forever, unattended. Just kept away from people. The effects are clearly documented and understood, and no extravagant procedures of any sort are required to keep it from doing anything to anything else. This is the very definition of a Safe SCP.</p>
<p>Its potential to be used outside of containment or following a classification has no bearing on what it's originally classified as. The page you cited is talking about there being two categories of Keters after the fact; if Keter, then this Keter/that Keter. That's not a quality that makes an object Keter in the first place.</p>

